# Workflow

`main` is protected. Agents never merge and never force-push.

One issue, one branch, one pull request. Branch:
`<agent>/<issue_number>_<slug>`. Comment `claim` and add `in-progress`
before editing. Stay inside the issue's files.

Commit messages are Conventional Commits with a scope from `task`, `verify`,
`reference`, `taskfmt`, `tooling`, `docs`, `ci`, `deps`, `spec`.
Example: `feat(task): add example_000_smoke`. No attribution trailers.

Pull requests include: issue link, spec reference (`spec/...#anchor`),
contract changes (`none` or a list plus an ADR), `make check` output, what
is not verified, and open science questions. Aim under 400 changed lines
excluding `data/` and lockfiles; a larger diff needs a reason.

Rebase on `main` before review. Squash merge is the owner's action.
A task-format, public-API, or layout change adds `docs/adr/NNNN-*.md`.
Update `PROGRESS.md` when status changes.

Hooks in `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.claude/settings.json` are part of the
contract. Do not weaken them to finish a task.
